  {"id":"ge","upper":"Г","lower":"г","name":"гэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ge-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ge-name.mp3"},"example":"го́род","exampleMeaning":"city","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ge-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ge-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is geh; usually a hard g, as in go. The whole name is not added to a word."},
  {"id":"de","upper":"Д","lower":"д","name":"дэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/de-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/de-name.mp3"},"example":"дом","exampleMeaning":"house","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/de-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/de-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is deh; the word sound is d, with the tongue close to the upper teeth."},
  {"id":"ye","upper":"Е","lower":"е","name":"е","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ye-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ye-name.mp3"},"example":"еда́","exampleMeaning":"food","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ye-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ye-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is yeh. At a word's start it begins with y; after most consonants it signals softness. Unstressed е changes sound."},
  {"id":"yo","upper":"Ё","lower":"ё","name":"ё","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yo-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yo-name.mp3"},"example":"ёлка","exampleMeaning":"fir tree","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yo-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yo-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is yo. It starts with y here; after most consonants it gives a soft consonant plus o. Ё is normally stressed."},
  {"id":"zhe","upper":"Ж","lower":"ж","name":"же","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/zhe-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/zhe-name.mp3"},"example":"жук","exampleMeaning":"beetle","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/zhe-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/zhe-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name sounds like zheh. In words, a voiced sound like s in pleasure, made farther back in the mouth."},
  {"id":"ze","upper":"З","lower":"з","name":"зэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ze-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ze-name.mp3"},"example":"зонт","exampleMeaning":"umbrella","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ze-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ze-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is zeh; the word sound is z, as in zoo. It can also be soft."},
  {"id":"i","upper":"И","lower":"и","name":"и","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/i-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/i-name.mp3"},"example":"и́мя","exampleMeaning":"name","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/i-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/i-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is ee. A vowel close to ee in see, usually shorter; it normally makes the preceding consonant soft."},
  {"id":"short-i","upper":"Й","lower":"й","name":"и кра́ткое","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/short-i-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/short-i-name.mp3"},"example":"йо́гурт","exampleMeaning":"yogurt","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/short-i-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/short-i-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"Its name means short i, but й is a consonant: a quick y glide, as in yes or the end of boy."},
  {"id":"ka","upper":"К","lower":"к","name":"ка","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ka-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ka-name.mp3"},"example":"кот","exampleMeaning":"cat","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ka-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ka-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is kah; the word sound is k, with less puff of air than English k in key."},
  {"id":"el","upper":"Л","lower":"л","name":"эль","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/el-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/el-name.mp3"},"example":"ла́мпа","exampleMeaning":"lamp","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/el-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/el-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is el. In words, л has hard and soft l sounds; the next letter often tells you which."},
  {"id":"em","upper":"М","lower":"м","name":"эм","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/em-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/em-name.mp3"},"example":"ма́ма","exampleMeaning":"mother","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/em-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/em-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is em; the word sound is m, as in mum. It can also be soft."},
  {"id":"en","upper":"Н","lower":"н","name":"эн","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/en-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/en-name.mp3"},"example":"нос","exampleMeaning":"nose","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/en-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/en-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is en; the word sound is n, as in nose. This is not an English H."},
  {"id":"o","upper":"О","lower":"о","name":"о","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/o-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/o-name.mp3"},"example":"о́блако","exampleMeaning":"cloud","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/o-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/o-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is o. Stressed о is a steady rounded vowel, without an English oh glide; unstressed о often sounds closer to ah."},
  {"id":"pe","upper":"П","lower":"п","name":"пэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/pe-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/pe-name.mp3"},"example":"па́па","exampleMeaning":"father","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/pe-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/pe-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is peh; the word sound is p, with less puff of air than English p in pen."},
  {"id":"er","upper":"Р","lower":"р","name":"эр","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/er-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/er-name.mp3"},"example":"ры́ба","exampleMeaning":"fish","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/er-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/er-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is er; the word sound is a tapped or rolled r made with the tongue tip. It is not an English P."},
  {"id":"es","upper":"С","lower":"с","name":"эс","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/es-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/es-name.mp3"},"example":"сок","exampleMeaning":"juice","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/es-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/es-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is es; the word sound is s, as in sun. It does not stand for k."},
  {"id":"te","upper":"Т","lower":"т","name":"тэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/te-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/te-name.mp3"},"example":"торт","exampleMeaning":"cake","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/te-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/te-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is teh; the word sound is t, made near the upper teeth with little puff of air."},
  {"id":"u","upper":"У","lower":"у","name":"у","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/u-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/u-name.mp3"},"example":"у́тро","exampleMeaning":"morning","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/u-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/u-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is oo. In words, a rounded vowel close to oo in food, usually shorter. It is not English y."},
  {"id":"ef","upper":"Ф","lower":"ф","name":"эф","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ef-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ef-name.mp3"},"example":"флаг","exampleMeaning":"flag","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ef-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ef-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is ef; the word sound is f, as in flag. It can also be soft."},
  {"id":"kha","upper":"Х","lower":"х","name":"ха","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/kha-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/kha-name.mp3"},"example":"хлеб","exampleMeaning":"bread","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/kha-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/kha-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is khah. The word sound is like ch in Scottish loch: air flows past the raised back of the tongue."},
  {"id":"tse","upper":"Ц","lower":"ц","name":"це","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/tse-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/tse-name.mp3"},"example":"цвето́к","exampleMeaning":"flower","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/tse-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/tse-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name sounds like tseh. In words, ts is one joined sound, like the end of cats. Ц is normally hard."},
  {"id":"che","upper":"Ч","lower":"ч","name":"че","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/che-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/che-name.mp3"},"example":"чай","exampleMeaning":"tea","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/che-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/che-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is cheh. The word sound is close to ch in cheese, but softer; ч is normally soft."},
  {"id":"sha","upper":"Ш","lower":"ш","name":"ша","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sha-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/sha-name.mp3"},"example":"ша́пка","exampleMeaning":"hat","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sha-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/sha-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"The name is shah. The word sound resembles sh, with the tongue farther back; ш is normally hard."},
  {"id":"shcha","upper":"Щ","lower":"щ","name":"ща","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/shcha-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/shcha-name.mp3"},"example":"щётка","exampleMeaning":"brush","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/shcha-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/shcha-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"Say a long, soft sh followed by ah for the name. In words, щ is a long, soft sh, distinct from the harder ш."},
  {"id":"hard-sign","upper":"Ъ","lower":"ъ","name":"твёрдый знак","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/hard-sign-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/hard-sign-name.mp3"},"example":"объе́кт","exampleMeaning":"object","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/hard-sign-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/hard-sign-word.mp3"},"kind":"sign","note":"The name means hard sign. Ъ has no sound of its own; it separates a consonant from the y sound in е, ё, ю or я."},
  {"id":"yery","upper":"Ы","lower":"ы","name":"ы","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yery-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yery-name.mp3"},"example":"сыр","exampleMeaning":"cheese","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yery-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yery-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name and vowel sound have no exact English equivalent. Keep your lips unrounded and your tongue farther back than for и."},
  {"id":"soft-sign","upper":"Ь","lower":"ь","name":"мя́гкий знак","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/soft-sign-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/soft-sign-name.mp3"},"example":"дверь","exampleMeaning":"door","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/soft-sign-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/soft-sign-word.mp3"},"kind":"sign","note":"The name means soft sign. Ь has no sound of its own; here it makes р soft. It can also separate sounds or mark grammar."},
  {"id":"e","upper":"Э","lower":"э","name":"э","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/e-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/e-name.mp3"},"example":"э́то","exampleMeaning":"this / this is","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/e-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/e-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is eh. In words, a vowel close to e in bet, with no initial y sound."},
  {"id":"yu","upper":"Ю","lower":"ю","name":"ю","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yu-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yu-name.mp3"},"example":"ю́бка","exampleMeaning":"skirt","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yu-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yu-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name sounds like you. It starts with y here; after most consonants it means a soft consonant plus oo."},
  {"id":"ya","upper":"Я","lower":"я","name":"я","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ya-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ya-name.mp3"},"example":"я́блоко","exampleMeaning":"apple","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ya-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ya-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"The name is yah. It starts with y here; after most consonants it means a soft consonant plus ah. Unstressed я changes sound."}
